---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About — GaiaVerity" desc="GaiaVerity is a gardening and lawn care resource for people who want to work with their land — not against it.">

  <!-- ── Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section style="background:#eef4f0; padding: 80px 24px 0; position:relative; overflow:visible;">
    <div style="max-width:680px; margin:0 auto; position:relative;">

      <p class="font-sans" style="font-size:11px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:0.18em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#c98633; margin-bottom:28px;">
        About GaiaVerity
      </p>

      <h1 class="font-sans" style="font-size:clamp(44px,7vw,80px); font-weight:700; line-height:1.02; letter-spacing:-0.03em; color:#23312b; margin-bottom:0;">
        Grow<br/>something<br/><em class="not-italic" style="color:#5c7962;">real.</em>
      </h1>

      <!-- Overlapping image — bleeds 120px into next section -->
      <div style="margin-top:48px; margin-right:-80px; position:relative; z-index:2; border-radius:24px; overflow:hidden; height:420px; margin-bottom:-120px;">
        <img
          src="/grantfreelancecopywriter.jpg"
          alt="Chester Beard — GaiaVerity"
          style="width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover; object-position: center top;"
          loading="eager"
        />
        <!-- Gold accent bar overlapping bottom of image -->
        <div style="position:absolute; bottom:0; left:0; right:0; height:6px; background:#c98633;"></div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Story ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section style="background:#f7f5f0; padding: 160px 24px 80px; position:relative;">

    <!-- Decorative circle behind text -->
    <div style="position:absolute; top:80px; left:-60px; width:320px; height:320px; border-radius:50%; background:#eef4f0; z-index:0;"></div>

    <div style="max-width:680px; margin:0 auto; position:relative; z-index:1;">

      <!-- First paragraph — offset right -->
      <div style="margin-left:80px; margin-bottom:64px;">
        <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:19px; line-height:1.85; color:#23312b;">
          I learned to garden from a man who refused to fight his own yard.
        </p>
        <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:19px; line-height:1.85; color:#23312b; margin-top:28px;">
          My father started gardening organically in the 1960s. Back then, almost
          nobody did. The garden aisle sold a spray for every problem, and most
          neighbors used all of them.
        </p>
        <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:19px; line-height:1.85; color:#23312b; margin-top:28px;">
          He went the other way. We had a small lot in Everett, Washington, and
          he dug wet garbage into the soil. Kitchen scraps, coffee grounds,
          whatever was left over. He fed the soil instead of the plant. No
          chemical fertilizers. Just organic matter, turned in by hand.
        </p>
        <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:19px; line-height:1.85; color:#23312b; margin-top:28px;">
          He made me help. I was the one turning the pile before school,
          complaining about the smell. He never explained why. He just said,
          "The soil will do the work if you let it."
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Floating label — offset left, breaking the column -->
      <div style="margin-left:-40px; margin-bottom:32px; display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:12px;">
        <div style="width:40px; height:2px; background:#c98633;"></div>
        <span class="font-sans" style="font-size:11px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:0.18em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#c98633;">
          What he taught me
        </span>
      </div>

      <!-- Second paragraph — offset left -->
      <div style="margin-right:80px; margin-bottom:80px;">
        <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:19px; line-height:1.85; color:#23312b;">
          The lesson was simple. You do not control nature. You work with it.
        </p>
        <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:19px; line-height:1.85; color:#23312b; margin-top:28px;">
          That sounds soft. It is not. It means you watch before you act. You ask
          why the moss is there before you kill it. You accept that some years the
          slugs win a row of lettuce.
        </p>
        <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:19px; line-height:1.85; color:#23312b; margin-top:28px;">
          It also means less work over time. Healthy soil does a lot of the job
          for you. A yard that fits its climate needs less water, less feeding,
          and less of your weekend.
        </p>
        <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:19px; line-height:1.85; color:#23312b; margin-top:28px;">
          It took me years to see how far ahead of his time he was.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Why GaiaVerity ─────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section style="background:#f7f5f0; padding: 0 24px 80px; position:relative;">
    <div style="max-width:680px; margin:0 auto;">

      <!-- Floating label — offset right -->
      <div style="margin-left:80px; margin-bottom:32px; display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:12px;">
        <div style="width:40px; height:2px; background:#c98633;"></div>
        <span class="font-sans" style="font-size:11px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:0.18em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#c98633;">
          Why I built GaiaVerity
        </span>
      </div>

      <!-- Content — offset left -->
      <div style="margin-right:80px; margin-bottom:80px;">
        <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:19px; line-height:1.85; color:#23312b;">
          I'm Chester Beard. I garden in Everett, Washington, and I've spent 20
          years working in sustainability, including a seat on the Sierra Club's
          Washington State Executive Council from 2005 to 2007.
        </p>
        <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:19px; line-height:1.85; color:#23312b; margin-top:28px;">
          Over those years I've read a lot of gardening advice that treats the
          yard as an enemy. Kill this. Spray that. Start over every spring. My
          father's garden proved there was another way, decades before it was
          popular.
        </p>
        <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:19px; line-height:1.85; color:#23312b; margin-top:28px;">
          GaiaVerity is where I write that approach down. Lawn alternatives.
          Mushrooms in the grass and why they usually belong there. Ground covers
          that survive a dry summer. Pest control that does not wreck everything
          else.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Pull quote — asymmetric card ──────────────────── -->
  <section style="background:#f7f5f0; padding: 0 24px 80px; position:relative;">
    <div style="max-width:680px; margin:0 auto;">

      <!-- Card breaks right edge -->
      <div style="margin-right:-48px; border-radius:24px; padding:56px 64px; background:#23312b; position:relative; overflow:hidden;">
        <div style="position:absolute; top:-60px; right:-60px; width:240px; height:240px; border-radius:50%; background:#2e4038;"></div>
        <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:clamp(20px,2.5vw,26px); line-height:1.6; color:#eef4f0; font-style:italic; position:relative; z-index:1; margin-bottom:28px;">
          "You do not control nature. You work with it."
        </p>
        <cite class="font-sans" style="font-size:11px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:0.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#80bea4; font-style:normal;">
          — Chester's father
        </cite>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Values — staggered single column ──────────────── -->
  <section style="background:#f7f5f0; padding: 0 24px 80px;">
    <div style="max-width:680px; margin:0 auto;">

      <p class="font-sans" style="font-size:11px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:0.18em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#c98633; margin-bottom:48px;">
        What you can expect here
      </p>

      <!-- Value 1 — indented right -->
      <div style="margin-left:60px; margin-bottom:48px; padding-bottom:48px; border-bottom: 1px solid #d8e5dc;">
        <span class="font-sans" style="font-size:11px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.12em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#80bea4;">01</span>
        <h3 class="font-sans" style="font-size:24px; font-weight:600; color:#23312b; margin:12px 0 14px;">Honest tradeoffs</h3>
        <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:#5c7962;">
          A clover lawn is not maintenance free. A meadow looks rough in its second year. I'll tell you that up front.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Value 2 — indented left (breaks left edge slightly) -->
      <div style="margin-right:60px; margin-left:-20px; padding-left:20px; margin-bottom:48px; padding-bottom:48px; border-bottom: 1px solid #d8e5dc;">
        <span class="font-sans" style="font-size:11px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.12em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#80bea4;">02</span>
        <h3 class="font-sans" style="font-size:24px; font-weight:600; color:#23312b; margin:12px 0 14px;">Backyard scale</h3>
        <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:#5c7962;">
          I write for people with a regular lot, a regular budget, and limited time.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Value 3 — wider, centered -->
      <div style="margin-bottom:48px; padding-bottom:48px; border-bottom: 1px solid #d8e5dc;">
        <span class="font-sans" style="font-size:11px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.12em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#80bea4;">03</span>
        <h3 class="font-sans" style="font-size:24px; font-weight:600; color:#23312b; margin:12px 0 14px;">Regional and seasonal detail</h3>
        <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:#5c7962;">
          I garden in the Pacific Northwest, and it shows. The principles travel. I'll say so when the timing does not.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Value 4 — indented right (mirrors Value 1) -->
      <div style="margin-left:60px; margin-bottom:48px; padding-bottom:48px;">
        <span class="font-sans" style="font-size:11px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.12em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#80bea4;">04</span>
        <h3 class="font-sans" style="font-size:24px; font-weight:600; color:#23312b; margin:12px 0 14px;">Free guides</h3>
        <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:#5c7962;">
          No account and no paywall. Some links are affiliate links, which means I may earn a commission at no cost to you. I only link to products that fit the approach.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Second photo — offset left ────────────────────── -->
  <section style="background:#f7f5f0; padding: 0 24px 80px;">
    <div style="max-width:680px; margin:0 auto;">
      <div style="margin-left:-48px; border-radius:24px; overflow:hidden; height:360px; position:relative;">
        <img
          src="/hands-in-soil.jpg"
          alt="Hands working soil in a backyard garden"
          style="width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover;"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <!-- Overlapping label card -->
        <div style="position:absolute; bottom:24px; right:24px; background:#f7f5f0; border-radius:16px; padding:20px 28px;">
          <p class="font-sans" style="font-size:12px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:0.12em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c7962;">Sustainable backyard</p>
          <p class="font-sans" style="font-size:12px; color:#80bea4; margin-top:4px;">grown from real soil</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── CTA ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section style="background:#eef4f0; padding: 80px 24px;">
    <div style="max-width:680px; margin:0 auto; text-align:center;">
      <h2 class="font-sans" style="font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,42px); font-weight:600; color:#23312b; margin-bottom:16px; letter-spacing:-0.02em;">
        Start here
      </h2>
      <p class="font-serif" style="font-size:17px; line-height:1.8; color:#5c7962; max-width:440px; margin:0 auto 36px;">
        Browse the guides or start with Lawn Alternatives, the most popular place to begin.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/blog/lawn-alternatives/"
        class="font-sans"
        style="display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; background:#23312b; color:#f7f5f0; border-radius:999px; padding:16px 36px; font-size:15px; font-weight:600; text-decoration:none;">
        Start with Lawn Alternatives
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
